description.narrative:
In its Observation adopted published  in 2023 on the application of the Equal Remuneration Convention, 1951 (No. 100), the Committee of Experts noted with satisfaction that section 244 of the new Labour Code, which was adopted in March 2022 and entered into force on 30 April 2023, appropriately reflected the principle of  “ensuring equal pay for men and women for work of equal value”. The Committee also noted the adoption on 2 September 2019 of Law No. LRU-562 on guarantees with respect to equal rights and opportunities for women and men. The ILO provided the following technical assistance:
- Preparation of an Issues Paper (2018) on key elements necessary for reform in the preparation of the comprehensive reform of the Labour Code, which identified the gaps between ILS and national legislation, including provisions of C100; 
- Provision of technical guidance on draft provisions of Labour Code regarding equality; 
- Preparation and dissemination of a Technical Memorandum on the draft Labour Code with clear recommendations on equal pay for work of equal value;
- Discussion / meetings with tripartite constituents to discuss contents of the TM, including recommendations and rationale for legislative reform to strengthen alignment with C100;
- Advocacy and training on C100 (various online and in-person events).
